Data Structures
│
├── 1. Primitive Data Types (int, float, char, pointers)
│
└── 2. Non-Primitive Data Structures
    │
    ├── A. Linear Data Structures (Elements arranged sequentially)
    │   ├── Static (Fixed size at compile time)
    │   │   └── Array
    │   │
    │   └── Dynamic (Size can grow/shrink at runtime)
    │       ├── Linked List (Singly, Doubly, Circular)
    │       ├── Stack (Can be implemented using Arrays or Linked Lists)
    │       └── Queue (Simple, Circular, Priority, Deque)
    │
    └── B. Nonlinear Data Structures (Elements arranged hierarchically or in networks)
        ├── Trees (Binary Trees, BST, AVL Trees) [Unit III of your syllabus]
        └── Graphs (Directed, Undirected, Weighted) [Unit III of your syllabus]
